ed to be changed as often as dirty underwear: regularly.</p>\n<p>Furthermore, this creates a problem for the good guys that get into politics. They usually don't last. They do their job, then leave their office better than when they found it. Same as any person with character would do. So with someone like Trump, who's had a successful life and has no real reason to get into politics, he presents the best possible scenario. Someone with experience and desire to truly help, then he'll leave. This is the type of politicians we need.</p>"],[2,5998103,5996514,3,0,3,"2016-08-05T19:10:25","Gorillion","",[],"<p>Fucking hell. Bill and Don are the same age. I know being president takes a toll on the body and nervous system. But holy fuck.</p>"],[1,5996730,0,17,0,17,"2016-08-05T16:39:45","Dereliction","",[],"<p>Wait ... Bush Jr. endorsed Hillary? Did this really happen? </p>"],[1,5996979,0,4,0,4,"2016-08-05T17:07:29","fagnig","",[],"<p>Well shes basically a neocon herself, why wouldnt he</p>"],[1,5998485,0,0,0,0,"2016-08-05T19:52:03","twentyfive","",[],"<p>didnt he paint himself in a bathtub.</p>"]]
